athbb Zy+\\\\mathbb Zh)\\\\otimes_{\\\\mathbb Z}K\\\\)\\nacts by the induced lattice operators. This is the Chevalley\\n\\\\(\\\\mathfrak{sl}_2\\\\) construction also in characteristic 2.\\nProve that \\\\(V(K)\\\\) is nonzero and every \\\\(K\\\\)-linear subspace\\ninvariant under \\\\(x,y,h\\\\) is zero or all of \\\\(V(K)\\\\).\\nBoth \\\\(\\\\lambda=0\\\\) and \\\\(p=2\\\\) are included; \\\\(K\\\\) need not be\\nalgebraically closed.\", \"conclusion\": \"V_K is nonzero, and for every K-linear subspace W⊆V_K, if W is invariant under the induced x,y,h then W={0} or W=V_K. Equivalently V(K) is irreducible as an L(K)-module. This holds for every given prime p, field K of characteristic p, integer 0≤λ<p, and arbitrary admissible lattice M, including λ=0 and p=2, without assuming K algebraically closed.\", \"parameters\": [{\"symbol\": \"p\", \"type\": \"natural number\"}, {\"symbol\": \"K\", \"type\": \"field\"}, {\"symbol\": \"λ\", \"type\": \"integer\"}, {\"symbol\": \"V\", \"type\": \"complex vector space\"}, {\"symbol\": \"x\", \"type\": \"element of the complex Lie algebra sl₂(ℂ)\"}, {\"symbol\": \"y\", \"type\": \"element of the complex Lie algebra sl₂(ℂ)\"}, {\"symbol\": \"h\", \"type\": \"element of the complex Lie algebra sl₂(ℂ)\"}, {\"symbol\": \"v\", \"type\": \"vector of V\"}, {\"symbol\": \"M\", \"type\": \"additive subgroup of V\"}], \"hypotheses\": [{\"id\": \"H001\", \"statement\": \"p is a prime number and K has characteristic p.\", \"origin\": \"problem.md:16-17\"}, {\"id\": \"H002\", \"statement\": \"λ is an integer satisfying 0≤λ<p.\", \"origin\": \"problem.md:16-17\"}, {\"id\": \"H003\", \"statement\": \"V is the complex irreducible highest-weight sl₂(ℂ)-module of highest weight λ, of complex dimension λ+1. The Chevalley generators x,y,h of sl₂(ℂ) act on V and satisfy [h,x]=2x, [h,y]=−2y, [x,y]=h. In its universal enveloping algebra and in the induced operators on V, the bracket is [a,b]=ab−ba; the same symbols denote the corresponding operators