algebra of U(sl₂(ℂ)) generated by X_r=x^r/r! and Y_r=y^r/r! for all natural numbers r. Its action on V is that induced by x,y,h.\", \"depends_on\": [\"D003\", \"D004\"], \"requires\": [], \"objects\": [\"V\", \"x\", \"y\", \"h\", \"X\", \"Y\"], \"binders\": [{\"symbol\": \"r\", \"type\": \"natural number\"}]}, {\"id\": \"D006\", \"symbol\": \"e\", \"type\": \"I-indexed family of vectors of V\", \"definition\": \"e_i=y^i v/i!=Y_i v for i∈I.\", \"depends_on\": [\"D002\", \"D004\"], \"requires\": [], \"objects\": [\"I\", \"v\", \"y\", \"Y\"], \"binders\": [{\"symbol\": \"i\", \"type\": \"element of I\"}]}, {\"id\": \"D007\", \"symbol\": \"R\", \"type\": \"subring of ℚ and hence of ℂ\", \"definition\": \"R=ℤ_(p)={a/b∈ℚ:a,b∈ℤ, b≠0, p∤b}, with its usual subring operations.\", \"depends_on\": [], \"requires\": [\"H001\"], \"objects\": [\"p\"], \"binders\": [{\"symbol\": \"a\", \"type\": \"integer\"}, {\"symbol\": \"b\", \"type\": \"integer\"}]}, {\"id\": \"D008\", \"symbol\": \"M_R\", \"type\": \"R-module\", \"definition\": \"M_R=R⊗_ℤ M.\", \"depends_on\": [\"D007\"], \"requires\": [\"H001\"], \"objects\": [\"R\", \"M\"], \"binders\": []}, {\"id\": \"D009\", \"symbol\": \"iota\", \"type\": \"R-linear map M_R→V (V restricted to R)\", \"definition\": \"iota(r⊗m)=rm for r∈R and m∈M; its image is the R-span of M. Identification of M_R with this image is made only after its injectivity is proved.\", \"depends_on\": [\"D007\", \"D008\"], \"requires\": [\"H001\"], \"objects\": [\"R\", \"M_R\", \"M\", \"V\"], \"binders\": [{\"symbol\": \"r\", \"type\": \"element of R\"}, {\"symbol\": \"m\", \"type\": \"element of M\"}]}, {\"id\": \"D010\", \"symbol\": \"E\", \"type\": \"I×I-indexed complex-linear endomorphisms of V\", \"definition\": \"E_ij is the unique complex-linear map taking e_j to e_i and all e_k with k∈I and k≠j to zero. This construction is used only after (e_i) is proved to be a complex basis.\", \"depends_on\": [\"D002\", \"D006\"], \"requires\": [\"N001\"], \"objects\": [\"V\", \"I\", \"e\"], \"binders\": [{\"symbol\": \"i\", \"type\": \"element of I\"}, {\"symbol\": \"j\", \"type\": \"element of I\"}, {\"symbol\": \"k\", \"type\": \"element of I\"}]}, {\"id\": \"D011\", \"symbol\": \"Pi\", \"type\": \"complex-linear endomorphism of V\", \"definition\": \"Pi=Y_λ X_λ. This is the operator denoted P in the supplied proof; Pi avoids confusion with the target proposition ID P.\", \"depends_on\": [\"D003\", \"D004\"], \"requires\": [\"H002\"], \"objects\": [\"Y\", \"X\", \"λ\"], \"binders\": []}, {\"id\": \"D012\", \"symbol\": \"J_i\", \"type\": \"I-indexed R-submodules of ℂ\", \"definition\": \"For i∈I, J_i={c∈ℂ:c e_i∈iota(M_R)}.\", \"depends_on\": [\"D002\", \"D006\", \"D007\", \"D008\", \"D009\"], \"requires\": [\"H001\"], \"objects\": [\"I\", \"e\", \"R\", \"iota\", \"M_R\"], \"binders\": [{\"symbol\": \"i\", \"type\": \"element of I\"}, {\"symbol\": \"c\", \"type\": \"complex number\"}]}, {\"id\": \"D013\", \"symbol\": \"J\", \"type\": \"R-submodule of ℂ\", \"definition\": \"J=J_0; the index 0 belongs to I since 0≤λ.\", \"depends_on\": [\"D012\"], \"requires\": [\"H001\", \"H002\"], \"objects\": [\"J_i\", \"I\", \"λ\"], \"binders\": []}, {\"id\": \"D014\", \"symbol\": \"V_K\", \"type\": \"K-vector space\", \"definition\": \"V_K=V(K)=M⊗_ℤ K, with x,y,h acting by their induced lattice operators when their preservation of M is established.\", \"depends_on\": [], \"requires\": [], \"objects\": [\"M\", \"K\", \"x\", \"y\", \"h\"], \"binders\": []}, {\"id\": \"D015\", \"symbol\": \"L_K\", \"type\": \"Lie algebra over K\", \"definition\": \"L_K=L(K)=(ℤx+ℤy+ℤh)⊗_ℤ K, formed from the abstract Chevalley generators in sl₂(ℂ), with bracket induced by [h,x]=2x, [h,y]=−2y, [x,y]=h. Once preservation of the lattice by these operators is established, its action on V_K is the tensor extension of that lattice action. This is the Chevalley construction also when p=2.\", \"depends_on\": [\"D014\"], \"requires\": [\"H003\"], \"objects\": [\"K\", \"p\", \"x\", \"y\", \"h\", \"V_K\"], \"binders\": []}, {\"id\": \"D016\", \"symbol\": \"F_p\", \"type\": \"prime subfield of K identified with ℤ/pℤ\", \"definition\": \"F_p=ℤ/pℤ, embedded in K by the integer map.\", \"depends_on\": [], \"requires\": [\"H001\"], \"objects\": [\"p\", \"K\"], \"binders\": []}, {\"id\": \"D017\", \"symbol\": \"kappa\", \"type\": \"ring map R→K\", \"definition\": \"For a/b∈R with p∤b, kappa(a/b)=(a·1_K)(b·1_K)^(-1). Denominators are nonzero since K has characteristic p; cross multiplication makes the expression independent of its representation.\", \"depends_on\": [\"D007\"], \"requires\": [\"H001\"], \"objects\": [\"R\", \"K\", \"p\"], \"binders\": [{\"symbol\": \"a\", \"type\": \"integer\"}, {\"symbol\": \"b\", \"type\": \"integer\"}]}], \"logic\": {\"classical\": true, \"rules\": [\"direct\", \"natural_induction\", \"forall_introduction\", \"implication_introduction\", \"exists_elimination\", \"case_elimination\"], \"calculations\": [\"equality\", \"definitions\", \"finite_algebra\", \"finite_order\", \"finite_sums\"], \"primitives\": [{\"symbol\": \"0\", \"type\": \"typed numeral\", \"meaning\": \"Zero of the explicitly specified mathematical type.\"}, {\"symbol\": \"1\", \"type\": \"typed numeral\", \"meaning\": \"One of the explicitly specified mathematical type.\"}, {\"symbol\": \"2\", \"type\": \"typed numeral\", \"meaning\": \"Two of the explicitly specified mathematical type, including an exponent two.\"}, {\"symbol\": \"ℕ\", \"type\": \"number system\", \"meaning\": \"The natural numbers with their usual arithmetic.\"}, {\"symbol\": \"ℤ\", \"type\": \"number system\", \"meaning\": \"The integers with their usual arithmetic.\"}, {\"symbol\": \"ℚ\", \"type\": \"number system\", \"meaning\": \"The rational numbers with their usual ordered-field operations.\"}, {\"symbol\": \"ℝ\", \"type\": \"number system\", \"meaning\": \"The real numbers with their usual ordered-field structure.\"}, {\"symbol\": \"ℂ\", \"type\": \"number system\", \"meaning\": \"The complex numbers with their usual field structure.\"}, {\"symbol\": \"∅\", \"type\": \"typed set notation\", \"meaning\": \"The empty set in the explicitly specified ambient type.\"}, {\"symbol\": \"∞\", \"type\": \"typed order notation\", \"meaning\": \"The top element in an explicitly specified extended ordered codomain.\"}]}, \"pins\": {\"lean_version\": \"4.32.2\", \"mathlib_commit\": \"905b95818eb32af7874a58b427f50c1711a5e96c\", \"mathlib_root\": \"/Users/syyui/formalization-tools/lean-mathlib-v4.32.2/mathlib\"}, \"inputs\": [{\"path\": \"inputs/problem.md\", \"sha256\": \"7e8b2dbb14d29165e887ffc8e291c0c7620070a122e1179ce63944ab1b3223ca\"}, {\"path\": \"inputs/target-selection.json\", \"sha256\": \"b7b636ec721dbad65cf9112bb6fa35caaa40483a0d781f8a688c1adbea7802ca\"}]}, \"has_more\": false, \"next_offset\": null}"}}
